\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\f0\fs24\cf0
\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s it!\u8221\'94 Vigram shouted. Below, in the leech lake, two leechmen tried to force the ox\u8217\'92s snout into a bag of freeweed smoke. \u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s IT!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram rushed to the edge of the patio. His eyes flew wide when the yellow-headed ox bucked both leechmen off its back. With another hip-shift and buck, the ox broke its constraints, then jumped its rail. The beast tore through the leech lake, kicking up waves of confused, copulating leeches.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Stop that ox!\u8221\'94 Vigram shouted as he pointed with his loaded brush. \u8220\'93There\u8217\'92s three silver-strings of leeches attached to that beast! If you don\u8217\'92t\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram,\u8221\'94 Lora moaned from her seat. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re rich already. Let it go.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t ask me to let go of my principles,\u8221\'94 Vigram replied. \u8220\'93That beast is }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 defies}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  me!\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram stomped back towards the canvas. He set his brush down on the palette, not caring that it rolled into a swatch of blue. Ever the man of action, he marched down to the leech lakes to slap his lazy leechmen. He ordered them after the ox. He screamed at them, bald head rumpling, but his screaming only worked against him, for it stirred a few bleeding cows and goats out of their drug induced reverie. Their horrid shrieks woke up others, and they shrieked too, a cascade of tortured screams. Vigram threw his head back and yelled right back at them. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93He\u8217\'92s an animal,\u8221\'94 Lora said as she slid off her stool.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You say you\u8217\'92re his }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 niece}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 ?\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 Mandri asked.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He scraped a slap of yellow ochre back into its little clay jar. There was enough untouched pigment left on the palette for at least four more of these awkward lessons.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora picked up Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s paintbrush and rolled its handle between her fingers. An awkward fidget.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So,\u8221\'94 Lora said. \u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t know anyone around here, and I don\u8217\'92t know you, but the fact that you obviously don\u8217\'92t want to be here either means you\u8217\'92re the only one I feel comfortable enough asking this: Do you have a place that I could stay? I have to get out of here.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri froze. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Uh,\u8221\'94 he muttered. \u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t, sorry. I mean, I do, but I don\u8217\'92t think you\u8217\'92d find it comfortable.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Dying shrieks. Vigram chewing it out.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Inquiring eyes.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I have a farm,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93There\u8217\'92s no house or anything. It\u8217\'92s mainly dirt. Like I said, I don\u8217\'92t think a girl like yourself would find it comfortable. You\u8217\'92d basically be sleeping outside.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll be fine. Let me get my things.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Stomped and sort of drifted  .  It wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t until she disappeared that Mandri remembered that she wasn\u8217\'92t what he was here for. He was here for the money. And neither did he want the company. He began to hate himself for not stopping her, because now he would have to tell her that what she thought was happening wasn\u8217\'92t. His legs began to sweat just thinking about it. His body was telling him to flee. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Faster than he expected, Lora stepped back out onto the patio, dressed in a long black robe. S}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 he wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t adorned with the usual veneer of civilization; no shine-silver bracelets, or gold hoop earrings, or rhombic beads, no makeup or red-threaded leaves trimming her robe. The only ornament on her entire body was the turtle-shell hilt of a dagger which she kept fashionably crooked in her waistband. The rest of her tawny self could have been slapped together in a reed hut on the banks of the river Jek, complete with splotches of mud dust staining the hem of her sleeves. She was dirty, with perfect teeth, shrouded in a sun-shade hood.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Mandri supposed it was some sort of traveling disguise. The fact that she would wear that just to escape Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s clutches said quite a bit.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m sorry,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93I can\u8217\'92t leave until I\u8217\'92ve been paid. That\u8217\'92s sort of why I\u8217\'92m here.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lora reached into her robe and pulled out a full silver string. The round coins jangled like little bells. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Is this enough?\u8221\'94 she asked.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t want to take your money,\u8221\'94 Mandri said.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s not mine.\u8221\'94 Lora tossed the full silver string at Mandri. \u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s Vigram\u8217\'92s. You can have it. There\u8217\'92s plenty more.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t think he would be happy if\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram is never happy. Now, are we leaving?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram chasing the ox into a thorny hedge.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I just don\u8217\'92t understand the urgency.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll show you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Walking off to the right, avoiding the water on the left.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri kept to the right. The lake on the left held leeches bigger than his arm. Instead of stalls penning in live animals, its banks were lined with bones. The lake\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s center was a constant swirl as hundreds of leeches swarmed just under the water\u8217\'92s surface, bunch-crawling like caterpillars, slithering like eels, desperate to get in a taste of whatever corpse had bothered to drop in. Mandri grimaced at the sight of it. Then, suddenly, a round shape popped out of that writhing mass like a buoy. It rotated around, revealing itself to be a severed head, somewhat fresh, a human head, complete with close cropped hair, an upturned nose, and an open mouth which could not scream. A leech latched onto its cheek, and as soon as that had come, it sank.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Nope!\u8221\'94 Mandri said to himself. \u8220\'93Nope, nope, nope,\u8221\'94 he repeated as he darted towards Vigram\u8217\'92s gate. Once onto the road, he quickened his pace. He didn\u8217\'92t feel out of reach until he crested the big hill that overlooked Vigram\u8217\'92s estate. Only then did he risk a look back. Lora was right behind him.\line \tab \u8220\'93Keep going!\u8221\'94 Lora said.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He walked all the way to Geem\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s and used his pay to buy half a bushel of burgeons. They were down-valley burgeons, decent stuff, but the waxy capsule leaves were liable to split. The insides would dry out before he could get to them in the ways that he wanted to. But, that was all Geem had, so he bought them.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He continued along the road, stomping his way through the muddy wheel-ruts, slapping away the flies, humming nursery rhymes, trying anything to distract himself from overthinking the sight of that severed head. Because it was only a severed head. That\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s all it was! It might have never belonged to a body, or been a person. There\u8217\'92s no way of knowing, really. Anything was possible. Besides, a rich man like Vigram was sure to accumulate enemies alongside the rest of his possessions. What was one little head?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri thought about his barren farm.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He thought about relaxing under his tree.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He thought about sipping a milky hooch spiked through with burgeon juice.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He would like to escape into that hooch. It would be bliss.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 ______}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 This girl, Lora, took an interest in him. It might be out of convenience, but, . She kept asking him questions, and he had a hell of a time not spinning it up into more than what it was. She asked him where he was from, why was he was here, why he didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t want to paint anymore. She claimed to have a friend who stopped because they\u8217\'92d gotten bored with it.  Mandri said, \u8220\'93that\u8217\'92s not me.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So, you don\u8217\'92t paint anymore?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why not?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93There\u8217\'92s no point. Every artist who has ever tried to capture the beauty of nature has failed. Why they even try is a mystery.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Beauty is out there in the world, and it\u8217\'92s connected to everything else. To truly capture it, you\u8217\'92d have to cut it out, and kill it, and that\u8217\'92s not possible. More than that, it\u8217\'92s wrong.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Mandri burped.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 He took another swig of the burgeon hooch that he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d left steeping in a jar. This jar was hidden in a hole halfway between Vigram\u8217\'92s rich leech farm, and his own failed bean farm. He had a few hidey holes like this, spread out along the way. He\u8217\'92d sip one hole\u8217\'92s hooch, and by the time he was finished, he\u8217\'92d arrived at the next. He replenished each stop with a little bit of water, sugar, and the burgeons he\u8217\'92d bought from Geem. This burgeon hooch was far from tasty, but it did the trick.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 He took another swig, then continued walking. He took a longer swig, then continued spiraling over the fact that he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d ever picked up a paintbrush.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You ever think about what a painting is, really?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Paint a tree, and all those leaves get reduced to flecks of green. A living leaf with all its complexity, its pattern, its anastomosing veins pumped full of vital fluids, its green birth and brown death, its fall from the branch, its decay into dirt, that whole nested universe, it all gets reduced to a fleck of green.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Is that wrong?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93The truth that no artist wants to admit is that art has nothing to do with truth, it is pure seduction. It\u8217\'92s about looking at }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1\cf1 this}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 , and explicitly }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1\cf1 not}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1  }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1\cf1 that}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 . Paint an oasis, and look, there\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s a naked woman bathing in the mossy water. Focus the viewer\u8217\'92s gaze by sharpening the droplets of jade that gleam on her cinnamon skin. The leaf? Feather its edge into the sky. Blame it on the effects of atmospheric haze. Better yet, don\u8217\'92t paint the leaf, paint bunches of leafy shapes! Think about removing the tree entirely, because it\u8217\'92s good practice to erase all evidence of a crime after it\u8217\'92s committed.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Look, stop and ask yourself, what kind of person looks at the wonder of creation and says to themselves, \u8216\'91People ought to know about }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1\cf1 my}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1  interpretation.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92 As if the world doesn\u8217\'92t speak for itself.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t know,\u8221\'94 Lora said. \u8220\'93I like to look at pretty pictures.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Then you\u8217\'92re an enabler,\u8221\'94 Mandri said as he downed the dregs. \u8220\'93You can\u8217\'92t encourage these people. Imagine going to see an art gallery. Reality is right outside, but you go }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1\cf1 inside}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1  to see it cornered, killed, flayed, then put on display, with choice sections of its hide stitched into pretty frames.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Nothing important is happening in art.  he would have liked to be successful.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Oh, well, he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s found us.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 Vigram, you\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92ve interrupted.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But I thought, I thought you said to\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8220\'93}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1}